# Attach an Elastic IP to an EC2 Instance Using Terraform

## Task Overview

The objective was to attach the existing Elastic IP `devops-ec2-eip-t1q3` to the EC2 instance `devops-ec2-t1q3` in the AWS `us-east-1` region using Terraform only.

## Working Directory

```text
/home/bob/terraform/t1q3
```

## Terraform Configuration

The existing `main.tf` file defined the EC2 instance and Elastic IP. An `aws_eip_association` resource was added to associate them.

```hcl
resource "aws_eip_association" "devops_ec2_eip_association" {
  instance_id   = aws_instance.ec2.id
  allocation_id = aws_eip.ec2_eip.id
}
```

The resource references use the IDs of the existing Terraform-managed resources rather than hard-coded identifiers.

## Execution Commands

